Lonely Runner endpoint-cycle formal session (codex-2026-05-31 S384)

FORMAL ENDPOINT-CYCLE REDUCTION
========================================================================================
Given a finite endpoint/interval system (E,I,B,P), draw an arrow e -> f when some interval protecting e has f as a boundary endpoint.
Every nonempty protection core has at least one outgoing arrow from each remaining endpoint, hence contains a directed endpoint cycle.
By THM-357 and THM-359, an LRC counterexample therefore must realize a directed cycle in the labelled integer endpoint-protection graph.

