ARITHMETIC LABEL GRAMMAR FOR THE NEXT SEARCH
========================================================================================
A protected endpoint cycle is not just e0 -> e1 -> ... -> e0.  Each arrow must carry an owner speed u, a protector speed p, a center m, and a sign eps satisfying the strict integer inequality

    | p*(n*m + eps) - a*n*u | < u

for some integer a.  The cycle-first search should enumerate these labelled inequalities, then ask whether their boundary intervals can also produce full measure.  That separates real LRC arithmetic from abstract circular-arc mirages.

NEW IDEAS GENERATED
========================================================================================
1. Endpoint-cycle rank: the length and slack profile of the first surviving protection cycle after partial peeling.
2. Arithmetic mirage filter: generate abstract all-protected cores first, then reject them by speed-orbit and integer-inequality labels.
3. Cycle slack potential: sum the strict margins u-|p*(n*m+eps)-a*n*u| around a cycle; prove primitive cycles have positive leak.
4. Unit-layer trap: any cycle touching unit endpoints must pass through speeds divisible by n, so quotient descent should start there.
5. Torsion shortcut test: product-sum/torsion coordinates may be exactly the short labelled cycles that almost close but expose higher endpoints.
6. LRC-TDA feature: terminal-core size is too coarse; record the largest preterminal directed cycle before its first endpoint leaf is removed.

